Subject: Rebuild the greedy-quantifier match position from the subject
Origin: Filnix
Upstream-Status: Not submitted
Applies-After: ports/patch/quickjs.patch

lre_exec_backtrack returns the end of a no_recurse match as an intptr_t,
and REOP_simple_greedy_quant casts it back to a pointer. Under Fil-C the
integer carries no capability, so the next character read traps. Every
simple greedy quantifier hits this: /a+/.exec("xaa"), /.*/.exec("abc").
Derive the position from the subject buffer instead; tests/quickjs.nix
covers it.

--- a/libregexp.c
+++ b/libregexp.c
@@ -2359,7 +2359,8 @@
                         return res;
                     if (!res)
                         break;
-                    cptr = (uint8_t *)res;
+                    /* res is an address inside the subject string */
+                    cptr = s->cbuf + ((uintptr_t)res - (uintptr_t)s->cbuf);
                     q++;
                     if (q >= quant_max && quant_max != INT32_MAX)
                         break;
